      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرَسٌ مُسْتَأْتٍ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتِىٌّ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْتًى</span></b> , and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مستوتى</span>,
[so I find it written, perhaps for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتَوْتٍ</span>, which
may be a dial. van. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتأْتٍ</span>, like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاتَيْتُهُ</span>is of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آتَيْتُهُ</span>,] <i>A mare desiring the stallion.</i> (TA.)

